// Ask a live node what stake two keys carry, and publish the two answers **as numbers**.
//
// The bond probe for #193's live arm, and its shape is the point rather than an accident. The first
// version of this arm published the whole pool and compared what the CLI rendered; that rendering is a
// derived `Debug`, so a key comes out as `GByteArray([2, 2, …])` — decimal — and the reading rested on
// a grep that could not match. Here the comparison is an `EMap` lookup in rholang and the reply is a
// number, which nothing can obscure.
//
// **The two answers are a measurement and its control.** The first is the operator whose key carries a
// delegation; the second is a genesis validator that has delegated nothing and must read exactly its
// own bond. A reply that is wrong in the same direction as a broken read is then visible — and a
// reading whose control is wrong is not a reading.
//
//   tools/devnet.sh deploy pos-bonds-check.rho && tools/devnet.sh query pos-bonds-check
new pos(`rho:rchain:pos`), ret in {
  pos!("getBonds", *ret) |
  for (@bonds <- ret) {
    @"pos-bonds-check"!(
      (bonds.get("<OPERATOR_PUBKEY_HEX>".hexToBytes()),
       bonds.get("<DELEGATOR_PUBKEY_HEX>".hexToBytes()))
    )
  }
}
